00:30:44.190 --> 00:30:46.070
Well, I haven't finished my drink just yet.

00:30:47.190 --> 00:30:48.820
Okay, finish it.

00:30:49.810 --> 00:30:51.890
Hey, look, as long as you're killing time, why don't you sit down?

00:30:52.030 --> 00:30:52.710
No, thanks.

00:30:53.630 --> 00:30:55.520
And if you don't mind, she's going with me.

00:30:57.280 --> 00:30:59.970
Mind, it's just that I'm not sure she...

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:19.150
wants to go exactly

00:31:31.210 --> 00:31:31.390
Ah!

00:32:00.920 --> 00:32:01.180
Hey!

00:32:01.690 --> 00:32:02.650
I'm out for two minutes.

00:32:02.770 --> 00:32:03.190
You got it.

00:32:03.310 --> 00:32:03.470
Hey!

00:32:34.330 --> 00:32:35.890
Well, that was quite a drive.

00:32:36.230 --> 00:32:37.850
Yeah, drive fast.

00:32:38.280 --> 00:32:40.020
Kind of takes your mind off of unpleasant things.

00:32:40.850 --> 00:32:42.330
Good an excuse as any, I guess.

00:32:43.200 --> 00:32:43.940
Want another drink?

00:32:44.340 --> 00:32:46.120
Don't tell me you've got a bottle in the glove compartment.

00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:47.140
Better than that.

00:32:50.980 --> 00:32:52.740
Well, all the comforts at home.

00:32:52.960 --> 00:32:54.410
Yep, be they ever so humble.

00:32:55.120 --> 00:32:56.720
Good news, Len.

00:32:57.150 --> 00:32:58.450
Thought we were going off the cliff.

00:32:58.760 --> 00:32:58.980
Here.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.120
Oh, it's a room.

00:33:02.840 --> 00:33:04.220
Besides, this will steady your nerves.

00:33:06.110 --> 00:33:06.270
Thanks.

00:33:09.650 --> 00:33:10.510
Here's to your good health.

00:33:11.260 --> 00:33:12.160
May you always have it.

00:33:20.850 --> 00:33:21.750
You're a strange guy.

00:33:22.140 --> 00:33:22.460
I am?

00:33:22.950 --> 00:33:23.170
Yeah.

00:33:24.290 --> 00:33:25.770
I can't figure out just why.

00:33:26.810 --> 00:33:27.490
You know, it's funny.

00:33:28.920 --> 00:33:29.680
But nowhere you...

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:34.810
Walked into a bar, bought me a drink, got into a fight.

00:33:36.480 --> 00:33:37.300
Now look where we are.

00:33:37.920 --> 00:33:39.470
Yeah, where are we?

00:33:39.860 --> 00:33:40.540
You know where I am.

00:33:41.660 --> 00:33:44.760
Sitting out here in a car by the beach with a man I only met an hour ago.

00:33:45.760 --> 00:33:47.280
I guess that's not so good, is it?

00:33:48.880 --> 00:33:49.620
Sorry you came?

00:33:53.940 --> 00:33:54.340
I like you.

00:33:54.480 --> 00:33:58.110
You think I'd come out here with you if I didn't?

00:33:58.210 --> 00:33:59.790
I guess not.

00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:02.740
Let's take a walk.

00:34:03.870 --> 00:34:04.130
Walk?

00:34:04.480 --> 00:34:05.360
Yeah, down by the water.

00:34:05.840 --> 00:34:06.600
It's a beautiful night.

00:34:10.510 --> 00:34:11.370
I'll race you to the water.

00:34:11.620 --> 00:34:12.980
Wait, I can't run into the field.

00:34:13.160 --> 00:34:13.480
Okay.

00:35:31.660 --> 00:35:33.100
That blanket going to work out all right?

00:35:44.950 --> 00:35:46.230
You don't look too bad at all.

00:35:47.460 --> 00:35:48.160
Perfect fit.

00:35:48.360 --> 00:35:49.680
Oh, but this wool blanket.

00:35:50.620 --> 00:35:51.120
What's the matter?

00:35:51.970 --> 00:35:52.590
Are you kidding?

00:35:53.080 --> 00:35:54.800
I've got practically nothing on under this.

00:35:56.400 --> 00:35:57.160
Take it off.

00:35:57.680 --> 00:35:58.480
Oh, sure.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:02.260
You would have forced me to be a gentleman and offer you my coat.

00:36:03.380 --> 00:36:06.330
But, uh, first you better have some of this.

00:36:06.760 --> 00:36:07.980
Don't you think we've had enough?

00:36:08.600 --> 00:36:10.480
We've already fallen in the water once today.

00:36:11.750 --> 00:36:12.770
Sorry about what happened.

00:36:13.060 --> 00:36:15.290
Forget it. I think it's kind of fun.

00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:17.430
That is, if I don't get pneumonia.

00:36:18.950 --> 00:36:20.370
Don't worry. That they can cure.

00:36:21.540 --> 00:36:23.760
Common cold that still baffles the medical profession.

00:36:25.610 --> 00:36:26.650
That, among other things.

00:36:31.500 --> 00:36:32.680
Of course, I could take you home.

00:36:33.340 --> 00:36:34.040
Don't be silly.

00:36:34.590 --> 00:36:35.750
I can't go home like this.

00:36:36.060 --> 00:36:38.140
We'll have to stay here until my clothes dry out.

00:36:39.540 --> 00:36:39.980
All right.

00:36:40.900 --> 00:36:43.340
I could use that coat now.

00:36:44.640 --> 00:36:45.160
All right.

00:36:45.380 --> 00:36:45.800
Trade you.

00:36:46.080 --> 00:36:46.840
Coat for the blanket.

00:36:47.480 --> 00:36:48.080
Come on, now.

00:36:48.790 --> 00:36:49.910
Put it around my shoulders.

00:36:50.550 --> 00:36:51.290
All right.

00:39:01.790 --> 00:39:02.370
Thank you.

00:39:30.650 --> 00:39:32.930
Gil?

00:40:01.120 --> 00:40:03.000
This is the end of the video.

00:40:03.310 --> 00:40:03.490
Thank you for watching until the end.

00:40:03.490 --> 00:40:03.650
See you in the next video.

00:41:30.540 --> 00:41:31.420
Oh, Gil.

00:41:33.260 --> 00:41:34.160
You shouldn't have come.

00:41:39.390 --> 00:41:40.210
What are you doing down here?

00:41:43.970 --> 00:41:44.230
Mother.

00:41:49.470 --> 00:41:50.210
What are you doing down here?

00:41:51.770 --> 00:41:53.410
You remember Dr. Jacob Hoffman?

00:41:54.810 --> 00:41:56.630
Oh, but you remember.

00:41:57.240 --> 00:41:58.740
He and your father went to school again.

00:42:00.060 --> 00:42:00.900
Dr. Buchel knows him too.

00:42:02.980 --> 00:42:03.640
So what?

00:42:04.940 --> 00:42:08.860
Dr. Hoffman's been studying radiation poison for a long time.

00:42:09.150 --> 00:42:10.550
He's been able to cure a lot of people.

00:42:12.020 --> 00:42:14.180
After you left, Dr. Buchel wrote him about you.

00:42:15.070 --> 00:42:17.490
We got a letter from him, and he's coming to help you.

00:42:22.320 --> 00:42:23.760
Don't you realize what this means?

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:25.260
He may be able to cure you.

00:42:27.430 --> 00:42:28.390
No use, Anne.

00:42:31.400 --> 00:42:32.480
I'm beyond helping.

00:42:33.980 --> 00:42:36.600
This thing I could do.

00:42:44.290 --> 00:42:50.360
Your life was offered to come here and examine you.

00:42:50.730 --> 00:42:52.130
You won't even have to leave the house.

00:42:55.340 --> 00:42:56.280
Be here this afternoon.

00:42:56.300 --> 00:42:57.560
I can drive him up to see you.

00:42:57.680 --> 00:42:57.840
Please.

00:43:00.800 --> 00:43:01.540
Won't do any good.

00:43:03.130 --> 00:43:07.010
Please, Gil, just give up.

00:43:09.240 --> 00:43:10.100
At least see him.

00:43:10.220 --> 00:43:11.280
He's come all this distance.

00:43:14.060 --> 00:43:16.320
Please, Ann, please, just let me alone.

00:43:17.620 --> 00:43:24.760
Don't you want to get well and live normally again?

00:43:31.720 --> 00:43:35.040
You know how it's been wondering about you, worrying and hoping.

00:43:37.160 --> 00:43:45.820
Please, Gil, if you don't care about yourself, please do.

00:44:01.340 --> 00:44:17.890
I doubt anything that way, Dr. Hoffman. My heart's all right.

00:44:18.840 --> 00:44:21.520
No, Gil, you must let us doctors play our games now, won't we?

00:44:22.380 --> 00:44:24.440
We are like actors, you know. We like to show off.

00:44:24.840 --> 00:44:27.600
It's all very well for you to joke about it. It's not very funny to me.

00:44:28.280 --> 00:44:29.300
I thought you were going to help me.

00:44:31.470 --> 00:44:34.130
From what I know of your case, things are not as bad as you have feared.

00:44:35.020 --> 00:44:36.940
We analyzed the isotope you're working on, Gail.

00:44:37.700 --> 00:44:39.640
Dr. Hoffman thinks he may be able to cure you.

00:44:40.020 --> 00:44:41.600
Yeah, I think there's definite hope.

00:44:42.330 --> 00:44:43.270
Do you really mean it?

00:44:43.370 --> 00:44:45.720
I wouldn't mislead you about a thing like that.

00:44:46.740 --> 00:44:49.080
I'll tell you how much it would mean for me to get well, Dr. Hoffman.

00:44:50.580 --> 00:44:54.390
The weeks I've been locked up in this mausoleum, unable to go out any time except at night,

00:44:54.490 --> 00:44:57.590
afraid of the sun and these horrible attacks.

00:44:58.850 --> 00:44:59.730
I'll do anything.

00:45:00.060 --> 00:45:00.980
Anything to get well.

00:45:01.610 --> 00:45:02.010
Anything?

00:45:02.480 --> 00:45:03.320
Yes, anything.

00:45:03.920 --> 00:45:04.500
All right, then.

00:45:05.120 --> 00:45:07.640
After a few days of preliminary observation here at the house,

00:45:07.740 --> 00:45:09.460
we shall take you to my hospital back east.

00:45:10.280 --> 00:45:10.980
But how?

00:45:11.140 --> 00:45:12.400
I can't go out in the sun.

00:45:12.400 --> 00:45:13.520
Not even for a little while.

00:45:13.720 --> 00:45:14.780
Oh, we'll make arrangements.

00:45:15.520 --> 00:45:17.780
But, meanwhile, you are not to leave this house.

00:45:18.020 --> 00:45:19.500
Not under any circumstances.

00:45:20.440 --> 00:45:21.200
Not even at night?

00:45:21.410 --> 00:45:22.610
Not even at night.

00:45:23.070 --> 00:45:25.530
After what happened last evening, there's too much risk.

00:45:26.730 --> 00:45:29.970
No doubt you are aware that the transformation came this time after...

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:32.520
a much shorter exposure to the sun than the first time.

00:45:33.450 --> 00:45:34.910
Yes, I know.

00:45:35.710 --> 00:45:38.350
Now, this is because the skin gets more sensitive

00:45:38.350 --> 00:45:39.410
as time goes on.

00:45:40.670 --> 00:45:42.390
If there should be a next time,

00:45:43.310 --> 00:45:45.850
you might find that it takes only a very brief exposure

00:45:45.850 --> 00:45:47.050
to the sun to change you.

00:45:47.650 --> 00:45:50.760
You might also find that it takes much longer

00:45:50.760 --> 00:45:51.680
to change your back.

00:45:53.610 --> 00:45:55.470
No more wandering at night, my boy,

00:45:55.550 --> 00:45:58.110
and no more drinking gets to the hospital.

00:46:37.130 --> 00:46:37.330
Thank you.

00:47:01.850 --> 00:47:04.480
Why, the great suspense.

00:47:06.930 --> 00:47:08.770
He jumped in his car and drove off.

00:47:09.410 --> 00:47:11.130
I've been out with some odd ones in my time,

00:47:11.190 --> 00:47:12.490
but he sure takes the cake.

00:47:13.240 --> 00:47:14.620
He didn't even bother to wake me up.

00:47:24.840 --> 00:47:26.020
You finally get back to town.

00:47:26.340 --> 00:47:27.160
I hitchhiked.

00:47:27.620 --> 00:47:29.520
And let me tell you, that was no fun either.

00:47:30.510 --> 00:47:34.290
I must have been standing there for nearly half an hour watching car after car go by.

00:47:35.000 --> 00:47:36.780
Most of them didn't even bother to look at me.

00:47:37.840 --> 00:47:40.460
I could have been standing there with my clothes off and we wouldn't even slow down.

00:47:41.970 --> 00:47:44.210
Finally, I managed to flag down an old guy in a truck.

00:47:45.240 --> 00:47:46.880
I hope you could see what was on his mind.

00:47:47.820 --> 00:47:49.420
But after last night, I'm cured.

00:47:50.060 --> 00:47:51.680
I'm going to stick with guys I know.

00:48:01.440 --> 00:48:02.220
Double bourbon, please.

00:48:21.020 --> 00:48:21.880
Remember me, honey?

00:48:22.320 --> 00:48:23.320
Believe me, Trudy, I...

00:48:24.590 --> 00:48:25.490
See you outside.

00:48:25.970 --> 00:48:26.750
Come on, man.

00:49:00.160 --> 00:49:01.840
Look at his face.

00:49:05.140 --> 00:49:05.620
Take a look.

00:49:07.130 --> 00:49:07.770
I'm going to...

00:49:09.460 --> 00:49:10.380
Can't leave him here.

00:49:10.940 --> 00:49:12.150
He's done this.

00:49:15.210 --> 00:49:21.740
Just hold on.

00:49:51.120 --> 00:49:56.250
Yes, it's my place.

00:49:56.840 --> 00:49:57.600
It's your place.

00:49:58.130 --> 00:49:59.090
Don't worry, they're not here.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:00.600
Thanks.

00:50:07.350 --> 00:50:07.870
How are you feeling?

00:50:09.440 --> 00:50:09.860
Hello, brother.

00:50:16.620 --> 00:50:19.030
Don't let the sunlight in.

00:50:19.460 --> 00:50:19.880
The what?

00:50:20.400 --> 00:50:21.140
It's just sunlight.

00:50:22.460 --> 00:50:23.580
It's bad for my eyes.

00:50:25.520 --> 00:50:27.500
As a matter of fact, I've been going to the doctor for some treatment.

00:50:28.490 --> 00:50:29.550
Then make yourself at home.

00:50:30.320 --> 00:50:30.660
Relax.

00:50:31.450 --> 00:50:31.690
Thanks.

00:50:32.280 --> 00:50:33.340
I'll go home right after dark.

00:50:33.560 --> 00:50:36.280
It's just, you know, the doctor advised me to stay out of the sun.

00:50:37.390 --> 00:50:38.070
Who's complaining?

00:50:39.440 --> 00:50:46.870
You can stay longer if you want, right?

00:50:47.050 --> 00:50:48.380
It's probably Lucy.

00:50:48.600 --> 00:50:50.590
She's always trying to borrow something.

00:50:52.220 --> 00:50:53.180
You better take it easy.

00:50:53.580 --> 00:50:54.460
You don't look so hot.

00:50:55.320 --> 00:50:56.200
I don't feel so hot.

00:51:00.220 --> 00:51:08.240
Hello, Trudy. Just thought I'd drop around to see how you were after the little excitement last night.

00:51:11.020 --> 00:51:16.040
So you were going to take him to a hospital, huh? He's been here all night.

00:51:16.360 --> 00:51:18.300
And what if he has? That's my business.

00:51:18.760 --> 00:51:19.560
And mine.

00:51:23.770 --> 00:51:27.240
We should have finished you off last night.

00:51:28.080 --> 00:51:29.870
All right, Richard. Step.

00:51:30.600 --> 00:51:32.550
George, honey, I know what you're thinking,

00:51:32.730 --> 00:51:34.210
but nothing happened here last night.

00:51:34.730 --> 00:51:37.320
I just decided to bring him home instead of the hospital.

00:51:38.180 --> 00:51:39.080
Nothing wrong in that?

00:51:39.530 --> 00:51:41.360
No, of course not, Trudy.

00:51:41.860 --> 00:51:44.440
Nothing wrong with that and a lot of other things you do.

00:51:44.460 --> 00:51:45.380
Look, I can explain it.

00:51:45.560 --> 00:51:47.020
He can't go out in the daylight, George.

00:51:47.740 --> 00:51:50.740
Knock it off. You're making a big mistake.

00:51:51.660 --> 00:51:53.330
Okay, let's go.

00:51:54.940 --> 00:51:57.010
Not that way. Out the back.

00:51:57.860 --> 00:51:59.180
I'll talk to you later.

00:52:08.800 --> 00:52:10.100
Hey, wait a minute. Let's go.

00:52:10.280 --> 00:52:11.140
Can't we talk this over?

00:52:15.050 --> 00:52:15.450
Move.

00:52:17.280 --> 00:52:17.760
All right.

00:53:00.830 --> 00:53:01.540
Thank you.

00:53:30.120 --> 00:53:30.340
Yeah.

00:54:31.980 --> 00:54:34.750
No, he must wait. That's all he can do.

00:54:38.000 --> 00:54:38.260
Gil.

00:54:39.290 --> 00:54:39.530
No!

00:54:46.810 --> 00:54:55.440
Help myself, Dr. McGill.

00:54:55.910 --> 00:54:58.770
Sure wasn't your fault, Gil. He forced you out with a gun.

00:54:58.950 --> 00:54:59.970
Nevertheless, I command...

00:55:00.460 --> 00:55:02.180
You murdered somebody.

00:55:03.110 --> 00:55:08.490
I can prove it was self attack.

00:55:08.690 --> 00:55:09.710
You don't seem to understand.

00:55:09.940 --> 00:55:13.310
No matter what we prove, it doesn't honor the fact that I wanted to kill him.

00:55:13.880 --> 00:55:15.220
I've devoted my life to Sawyer.

00:55:15.900 --> 00:55:16.600
Do you see what's happened?

00:55:17.080 --> 00:55:18.100
What good has it done me?

00:55:18.530 --> 00:55:19.890
What chance have I got to fight?

00:55:20.500 --> 00:55:21.560
Why should I be the one?

00:55:22.020 --> 00:55:23.400
Can you answer me that? Why me?

00:55:55.790 --> 00:55:56.850
CIRCUMGILD IS A SCIENT

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:04.860
There's a very fine line and any little thing can move it.

00:56:20.500 --> 00:56:23.800
What do you want?

00:56:29.810 --> 00:56:29.970
Yes.

00:56:30.500 --> 00:56:33.160
And please don't make it harder for me.

00:56:33.280 --> 00:56:34.320
No, please, let's go.

00:56:34.380 --> 00:56:35.380
There's nothing anybody can do.

00:56:35.560 --> 00:56:36.620
This is the literary of George Miller.

00:56:36.880 --> 00:56:38.280
I do a warrant for a threat.

00:56:38.640 --> 00:56:38.940
Get him!

00:57:00.890 --> 00:57:08.010
I hope you're both satisfied.

00:57:08.660 --> 00:57:09.740
He made a nice clean break.

00:57:10.460 --> 00:57:10.640
Yeah.

00:57:14.400 --> 00:57:15.440
Not what I would have wished.

00:57:15.810 --> 00:57:17.330
And he ran over one of my men in the process.

00:57:18.900 --> 00:57:21.310
Jacobs, call the state police and give him a full description.

00:57:21.940 --> 00:57:22.100
Right.

00:57:22.200 --> 00:57:23.480
And get an ambulance up here right away.

00:57:26.120 --> 00:57:26.380
He's dangerous.

00:57:27.160 --> 00:57:29.180
He's only dangerous because he is a sick man.

00:57:29.530 --> 00:57:29.970
Yeah, they're...

00:57:32.490 --> 00:57:34.050
I understand he ran over one of my men.

00:57:35.510 --> 00:57:36.750
Well, I've got to get back to headquarters.

00:57:36.850 --> 00:57:38.110
Is this doctor mind if I go with you?

00:57:39.060 --> 00:57:41.100
It's all right. I'll get my medical case.

00:57:41.220 --> 00:57:42.970
Do you want to come?

00:57:43.640 --> 00:57:43.900
No.

00:57:44.710 --> 00:57:45.950
I've got a triathlon chance.

00:57:46.750 --> 00:57:48.050
See if I can find it before they do.

00:57:48.700 --> 00:57:49.480
Let me go with you.

00:57:49.700 --> 00:57:51.140
No, I think you'd better come with me.

00:57:51.840 --> 00:57:53.120
They have to bring him in by force.

00:57:53.340 --> 00:57:55.240
We might need all the help we can give him.

00:57:56.350 --> 00:57:56.650
That's right.

00:57:57.390 --> 00:57:59.630
I don't stand much of a chance against the entire police force.

00:59:02.810 --> 00:59:21.160
In an accident, where? Did they get him? Well, did anyone see him? Thank you.

00:59:30.800 --> 00:59:33.380
They didn't even know whose car it was until they checked the registration.

00:59:33.690 --> 00:59:34.810
Didn't they try to stop him?

00:59:34.950 --> 00:59:35.730
He wasn't there.

00:59:36.140 --> 00:59:38.020
Somebody said they saw him running away from the accident.

00:59:38.540 --> 00:59:39.420
I guess he wasn't even hurt.

00:59:39.950 --> 00:59:42.750
Well, get all the extra men in need and start setting up roadblocks around the city.

00:59:43.100 --> 00:59:43.900
He won't get far.

01:00:04.410 --> 01:00:04.710
Thank you.

01:00:30.540 --> 01:00:32.060
Well, that was another report on your friend.

01:00:33.550 --> 01:00:34.250
Well, let's see.

01:00:36.480 --> 01:00:40.690
He was first reported buying gas just about here.

01:00:42.780 --> 01:00:45.440
Then somebody saw him right here.

01:00:47.330 --> 01:00:51.530
The last report placed him just about here.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:02.170
The guy's up. He worked by now.

